- Record 2292 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Intelligent Recommendations Feature Available for SAP Build Process Automation Tasks \nDescription: The new Intelligent Recommendations feature is now available for SAP Build Process Automation tasks.   Administrators can now create AI models to offer to the end users a confidence level for their SAP Build Process Automation tasks in the SAP Task Center Web app.  For more information, see Working with the Task List and Working with Intelligent Recommendations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-11\nValid as Of: 2024-09-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2293 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Deprecation of SAP Concur User v1 API\nDescription: The SAP Concur User v1 API is deprecated and will be decommissioned. This change impacts the SAP Concur connector version 1, which uses the User v1 API. To update to SAP Concur connector version 2, which integrates with the Identity v4 API, see Update Connector Version.  Additionally, as of September 15, 2024, SAP Concur will support the APJ1 data center. For more information, see SAP Concur.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: 26636\n\n--- Record 2294 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Mail Server Configuration\nDescription: You can configure Basic and OAuth authentication for custom mails server in the administration console for Cloud Identity Services. See Configure Custom Mail Server.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: 26636\n\n--- Record 2295 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: 26636\n\n--- Record 2296 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Central Business Configuration - bundle option documentation\nDescription: Documentation for SAP Central Business Configuration bundle option is now available.  See: SAP Central Business Configuration Bundle\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: 26636\n\n--- Record 2297 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Separation of Signing Key for SAML and OIDC Tokens\nDescription: Before this release, our SAML and OpenID Connect (OIDC) implementations shared the same signing key at the tenant level. With this release, the keys for SAML and OIDC are separated which enables you to rotate signing keys for one protocol without impacting the other protocol.  For more information about tenant configuration, see:      Tenant SAML 2.0 Configurations      Tenant OpenID Connect Configurations    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: 26636\n\n--- Record 2298 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Deprecation of SAP Concur User v1 API\nDescription: The SAP Concur User v1 API is deprecated and will be decommissioned. This change impacts the SAP Concur connector version 1, which uses the User v1 API. To update to SAP Concur connector version 2, which integrates with the Identity v4 API, seeUpdate Connector Version .  Additionally, as of September 15, 2024, SAP Concur will support the APJ1 data center. For more information, seeSAP Concur .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2299 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Central Business Configuration - bundle option documentation\nDescription: Documentation for SAP Central Business Configuration bundle option is now available.  For more information, see SAP Central Business Configuration Bundle. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: ", "4-09-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2299 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Central Business Configuration - bundle option documentation\nDescription: Documentation for SAP Central Business Configuration bundle option is now available.  For more information, see SAP Central Business Configuration Bundle. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2300 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2024.19\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data integration and data modeling.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2024.19. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-10\nValid as Of: 2024-09-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1591 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Standard Requirement Formula 67\nDescription: Support standard requirement formula 67 that always returns true in the context of the Pricing service.  See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1592 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Access Sales Records in Purchasing Tables\nDescription: Only condition tables and condition records with application ‘V’ (Sales) are considered by the Pricing service. For cases where condition records with application ‘V’ were stored in condition tables with application ‘M’ (Purchasing), those tables can now be added to the replication and will also be considered.  See: Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1593 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Consider Condition Record Descriptions\nDescription: For certain back-end releases it is possible to maintain a description on the condition record level that is then displayed in the pricing results instead of the condition type description. This applies only to non-variant conditions. The Pricing service supports the same mechanism. The feature will only be activated on request through a customer ticket on component LOD-CPS-PRC.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1594 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Correct Exchange Rate Type in Currency Conversion Trace\nDescription: The engine trace used to show an exchange rate type different from the one that was used during price calculation. For example, when the local currency is EUR and the document currency is USD, if the exchange rate type passed is M, but an alternative exchange rate type EURX is maintained in the customizing, the exchange rate is determined based on the alternative type. However, the currency conversion trace did not use to reflect this correctly and displayed the originally passed exchange rate type, M. This discrepancy used to cause confusion during the analysis using the trace information. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1595 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Document Pricing - Change the Source of a Pricing Document\nDescription: When creating a new pricing document with endpoint POST /documents, the owner or source of the document can be specified by providing the following data: The source application, the source type; for example quote, and the source id; for example quote number 49709821. That source information is stored with the pricing document.  The source information can be used as a filter criteria in the APIs to manage stored pricing documents.  New: the enhanced endpoint PATCH /documents  allows overwriting the source of a pricing document if needed.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1596 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Document Pricing – Stable Source Condition IDs When Copying Items\nDescription: When copying an item, the condition id of the source item used to be changed because of an unintended re-pricing of the source document. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1597 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Extension Concept - Custom Implementation of Unsupported Standard Routines\nDescription: Not all standard pricing routines that are available in the back end are also available in the Pricing service. If needed, customers can request the implementation of a missing routine, but SAP might reject this, because the routine is not considered as relevant for the use cases that the Pricing service addresses. In such a case, SAP can allow and enable the customer to use the Pricing service’s extension concept to implement the standard pricing routine on a project-basis. The feature will only be activated on request through a customer ticket on component LOD-CPS-PRC.  See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits and Extension Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1598 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Return Condition Record Validity\nDescription: New response structure validity for item conditions returned by stateless pricing and document pricing, which exposes"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_0c88a314e2ccd072708de04239a04c3717bd919c4d15002bbc2b4dc84c8da946_v2"}